        "show_head": true,
        "eyebrow": "Clarity",
        "heading": "Where Clarity Stops Being Visible",
        "intro": "Everything from VS2 upward looks identical in a ring. The money saved by not buying VVS on a stone nobody will loupe is better spent on cut, or on size.",
        "headers": "Grade | What you can see | Who it suits",
        "first_col_bold": true,
        "col1_width": 25,
        "note": "Position matters as much as grade. An inclusion under a claw is hidden for life; the same inclusion in the centre of an emerald cut, which has large open facets and nowhere to hide, is a different proposition. We look at every centre stone before recommending it.",
        "narrow": false
      }
